00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:58.670
photo I always start with a three-point
s-curve so for me it's three points

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.330
across the middle starting with the
shadows at the bottom the shadows

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:05.630
usually are bumped up a little bit just
to bring out that extra little bit

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:10.280
that's been lost in the details and then
dropping the blacks down a little bit

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:16.400
more so it starts to create that S shape
I normally don't touch too many of the

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.360
